## Winter tires in Alberta — the questions that get asked

**When should winter tires go on in Calgary?** Once daily highs sit consistently below 7°C, usually mid-to-late October. Seven degrees is a rubber-compound threshold, not a snow threshold — winter tires outperform all-seasons before the first snowfall. The city-wide rush runs mid-October to mid-November.

**When do they come off?** Around April, on the same 7°C line in reverse. Winter compound is soft by design and wears quickly once roads warm up.

**Are snow tires and winter tires different?** No. Two names for the same product. What matters is the 3PMSF marking — the three-peak mountain snowflake on the sidewall. M+S alone is not a winter tire.

**Are winter tires legally required in Alberta?** Not within Calgary or on Alberta highways generally. They are required on Highway 93 and the Trans-Canada through the mountains during the winter-tire period.

**Are studded tires legal in Alberta?** Yes, year-round, unlike British Columbia. Studs help on glare ice and cost noise and dry-road wear otherwise.

**Do all four tires need to match?** Yes — winter tires go on all four wheels, including on front-wheel drive. Mismatched grip front to rear causes the rear to break away in corners.

**Tire pressure in the cold?** Pressure falls roughly 1–2 PSI for every 5°C drop. Calgary chinooks can swing temperatures 20°C or more in hours, which moves pressure in both directions within a day.

## Local context

Calgary runs −15°C to −30°C from November to March. Chinooks cause rapid thaw-freeze cycles, which build black ice on routes such as McKnight, Glenmore and 16th Avenue. April and May are pothole season, the most common cause of bent rims and sidewall damage. Construction on Deerfoot Trail is a routine source of nails and screws. Highway 93 to Banff and the Trans-Canada through the mountains carry a winter tire requirement.

## Not offered — do not represent these as available

- **Used tires.** Prince Tires sells new tires only.
- **Wheel alignment.** Balancing and rotation are offered; alignment is a different service and is not performed here.
- Free installation is not offered. The value proposition is wholesale pricing plus the Price Match Guarantee.

